# Talon Gates of Madara: played as a land it triggers "up to one target creature phases out". Bot1 targets Bot2's Memnite (an
# opponent's creature is a legal target): it phases out and, as the permanent's controller, Bot2 gets it back in Bot2's own untap
# step (CR 502.1, 702.26c) - not before. On turn 5 Bot1 plays a second Talon (a different card) and targets nothing ("up to
# one"): Bot2's Memnite stays. One Talon taps for {C} (pool checked), and that {C} pays the other's {1},{T} for one mana of
# any color (chosen), the pool checked right after.

[Bot1 Deck]
Talon Gates of Madara
Talon Gates of Madara
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Talon Gates of Madara.Play
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.PhasedOut.Count = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.PhasedOut.Count = 0
? Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 1
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Talon Gates of Madara.Play
Bot1.Target()
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Talon Gates of Madara#1.Activate(Ability: {T}: Add {C}.)
? Bot1.Mana = {C}
Bot1.Battlefield.Talon Gates of Madara#2.Activate(Ability: {1}; Color: U)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
? Bot1.Mana = {U}

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Memnite
Bot2.PhasedOut.Count = 0
